Rāma drives far through remaining night --- Hears villagers curse lust-bound Daśaratha --- Hears them brand cruel Kaikēyī breaker of bounds --- Crosses Vēdaśruti toward Agastya quarter --- Crosses cool cow-rich Gōmatī to sea --- Crosses Syandikā humming with peacocks and swans --- Shows Sītā Manu-given populous Kōsala realm --- Longs to hunt again in Sarayū woods with parents
